-- title:
--   Connected part at an ordinary prime spans at most a line
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $p$ be a prime not dividing $M$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain which is a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra, $K$ a field which is a fraction field of $O$, the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structures forming a scalar tower, and assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O$. Write $J =$ [`ModularCurve.JOne M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group of the $q$-expansion model of $X_1(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with the module structure over [`ModularCurve.HeckeAlgOne`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L16) $= \mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Primes} \sqcup \mathbb{N}, \mathbb{Z})$ given by [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129), and let $T =$ [`TateModule p J`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15) be the group of sequences $(x_n)_{n}$ in $J$ with $p^n x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$, a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module. Let $A$ be [`ModularCurve.rationalHeckeAlgebraOne p J`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L212), the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{Q}_p}(\mathbb{Q}_p \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T)$ generated by the image of the Hecke algebra. The assertion: for every ring homomorphism $\Lambda : A \to K$ which sends the image of each $c \in \mathbb{Z}_p$ to $c$ in $K$, for every unit $a$ of $O$ with $\Lambda$ of the $p$-th Hecke generator equal to the image of $a$ in $K$, for every $K$-vector space $W$ and $K$-linear $f : K \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T \to W$ satisfying $f(t\cdot x) = \Lambda(t)\, f(x)$ for every element $t$ of the Hecke algebra acting through the base-changed Tate representation, and for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $P$, the $K$-dimension of the image under $f$ of the $K$-span of the elements $1 \otimes x$ with $x \in T$ such that [`ModularCurve.reductionQExpModL`](def/ModularCurve_QExpReductionModL.html#L312) at $P$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ kills every $x_n$ is at most $1$.
--
--   This is the connected half of Deligne's description of the local behaviour at $p$ of the Galois representation attached to a $p$-ordinary weight-two eigenform of level prime to $p$, phrased inside the Tate module of $J_1(M)$: the kernel of reduction at a place above $p$ contributes at most a line to any $\Lambda$-co-eigenspace. It feeds the construction of an ordinary line on which Frobenius satisfies the expected quadratic relation, in [`ModularCurve.exists_ordLine_frobenius_quadratic_mem_tateModule_jOne_quotient_of_isUnit_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_ordLine_frobenius_quadratic_mem_tateModule_jOne_quotient_of_isUnit_of_not_dvd).
